{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Now you shall see whether My word shall come to pass.</b> Rabban Gamliel, son of Rabbi Yehudah HaNasi, says: It is impossible to deal with the frivolous — since they seek only a pretext, you will not satisfy them; in the end they will find fault with you. If you give them large livestock, they will say 'we asked for small'; if you give them small, they will say 'we asked for large'; 'we asked for wild beasts and fowl'; 'we asked for fish and locusts.' He said to Him: If so, they will say that my hand is too short. He said before Him: I am going and appeasing them. He said to him: <b>Now you shall see whether My word shall come to pass</b> — that they will not listen to you. Moses went to appease them. He said to them: <b>Is HaShem's hand too short?</b> — ״Behold, He struck the rock and waters gushed forth״ (Psalms 78) and the continuation, ״Can He also give bread?״ They said: This is an evasion — He does not have the power to fulfill our request. And this is what is said: <b>And Moses went out and spoke to the people</b> — since they did not listen to him, <b>and he gathered seventy men, etc.</b> (see Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:27.914993417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}